hi there it's Kevin van ORD standing in  for reviewer josiah renauldi to tell you  about counter spy counter spy is a slick  operation it's responsive action and  movement keep the tempo moving at a  steady clip precise gunplay and melee  combat give you tactical freedom and  rich customization options give you new  ways to play it's procedurally generated  missions the short runtime and some  scattered glitches can bug you but  CounterSpy superb presentation and  satisfying executions make for an  excellent adventure regardless  it's counter spies simplicity that makes  it so instantly appealing the  side-scrolling missions have you jumping  and shooting your way through a series  of safeguarded rooms in order to grab  critical Intel natural cover provides  plenty of chances to slow down and pick  your shots but quickly popping off a few  rounds once you elevate suspicion can be  just as efficient you're encouraged to  silently snap necks and land headshots  but you're crafty spy has enough raw  firepower to deal with the repercussions  of being spotted it's easy to pick up  and play but that doesn't mean that the  game lacks depth peeking over cover  alters your perspective transforming  counter spy into more of a shooting  gallery than a 2d side-scroller leaning  against walls looks to fire at enemies  in the distance deepening the  environments this perspective shift  occasionally breaks of beauty mechanics  you might awkwardly wrap your arms  around guards who are standing in the  background for instance what does and  doesn't grab someone's attention might  also shift from one cover spot to the  next  still emptying rounds into enemies on  multiple planes without alerting a soul  is genuinely satisfying search the area  the most obvious armament to have at the  ready is your silenced pistol but if  things get hairy you do have options  collecting schematics unlocks new  weapons to take into the field so feel  free to pull out an assault rifle of  your mob by guards modifiers offer  advantages like greater endurance and  silent steps even when you run of course  everything costs a bit of in-game cash  and since purchased modifiers disappear  after you finish a level you have to  cleverly budget your resources but as  long as you play smart and explore you  won't be short on money getting spotted  won't result in mission failure but  there are consequences if you don't  practice restraint counter spy takes  place in an alternate cold war setting  so there's an ever-present threat of a  nuclear attack hanging over your head  it's a constant race against a doomsday  clock and getting caught will expedite  the launch it's your job to keep both  the imperialist States and the Socialist  Republic at bay by monitoring their  alert States the 60 setting is best  represented through counter spies smooth  jazz jingles and cel-shaded aesthetics  which are sharp on both the PlayStation  Vita and on consoles period-appropriate  uniforms and propaganda create a strong  sense of place while deep reds and blues  proved consistently striking regrettably  it's over before you've had enough no  two levels are the same so you can keep  rolling the dice before reaching the  game's conclusion in order to discover  fresh level geometry nonetheless it only  takes a couple of hours to reach the end  leaving you wanting a lot more it might  be short but CounterSpy is a satisfying  adventure with responsive gunplay and a  lovingly crafted presentation this is a  stealth game that makes you feel as  silent as you are deadly and it's  wonderfully holy refreshing  you
 

